@TUTORIAL: SDSF                                 !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  This short course shows what SDSF does and how you use it, panel by
}  panel. It takes about a quarter of an hour. For the details of a
}  command or a field, use the help: the Help key on any SDSF panel.
}
}  Press Enter to go through the course from the start, or type the number
}  of a part:
}
@     1 }Using the tutorial
@     2 }The SDSF panels
@     3 }Following a job
@     4 }Looking at output
@     5 }Acting on jobs: hold, release, cancel, purge
@     6 }Showing fewer jobs: ST, PREFIX and DEST
@     7 }A summary
}
}
}
}
}
}  Enter: part 1   T: help contents   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZSEL = TRANS(&ISFHCMD
                1,ISFTNAV
                2,ISFTPAN
                3,ISFTJOB
                4,ISFTOUT
                5,ISFTACT
                6,ISFTLIM
                7,ISFTSUM
                *,'?')
